                        <div id="expandable-content-cooktop" style="position: relative; margin-top: 15px;">
                            <div id="expandable-text-cooktop" style="max-height: 80px; overflow: hidden; transition: max-height 0.4s ease; line-height: 1.7; color: #444; font-size: 14px;">
                                
                                <h4 style="color: var(--blue); margin: 15px 0 10px;">Gas Cooktop Repair</h4>
                                <p style="margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Electrolux gas cooktop repair</strong> addresses burner ignition systems, gas valve controls, and flame adjustment components. Common issues include burners not lighting, weak flames, clicking igniters, and uneven heat distribution. We repair spark ignition modules, gas valves, burner caps, and safety switches. Our technicians are certified in gas appliance service, ensuring proper combustion and leak-free operation. We service all Electrolux gas cooktop configurations including 30-inch and 36-inch models throughout NYC.</p>

                                <h4 style="color: var(--blue); margin: 15px 0 10px;">Electric Cooktop Repair</h4>
                                <p style="margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Electrolux electric cooktop repair</strong> covers radiant and coil heating elements, touch controls, and glass surfaces. We diagnose heating element failures, control board malfunctions, and temperature regulation problems. Common repairs include replacing burned-out elements, fixing unresponsive touch controls, and addressing hot surface indicator failures. Our technicians repair all Electrolux electric cooktop configurations while protecting delicate glass-ceramic surfaces during service.</p>

                                <h4 style="color: var(--blue); margin: 15px 0 10px;">Induction Cooktop Repair</h4>
                                <p style="margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Electrolux induction cooktop repair</strong> addresses the electromagnetic technology providing precise, efficient heating. Induction cooktops heat cookware directly while keeping the surface cool. We repair induction coils, control electronics, cooling fans, and power systems. Common issues include zones not detecting cookware, error codes, and inconsistent heating. Our technicians understand Electrolux's FlexInduction® technology and the specialized components enabling induction cooking's instant response and safety features.</p>

                                <h4 style="color: var(--blue); margin: 15px 0 10px;">Radiant Cooktop Repair</h4>
                                <p style="margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Electrolux radiant cooktop repair</strong> services glass-ceramic surfaces with radiant heating elements beneath. We repair heating elements, thermal limiters, infinite switches, and touch control systems. Common issues include elements not heating, uneven cooking, and cracked glass surfaces. Our technicians diagnose radiant element failures, control board problems, and wiring issues. We handle glass-ceramic cooktops carefully to prevent surface damage during repair service.</p>

                                <h4 style="color: var(--blue); margin: 15px 0 10px;">Downdraft Cooktop Repair</h4>
                                <p style="margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Electrolux downdraft cooktop repair</strong> addresses integrated ventilation systems that retract when not in use. We repair pop-up ventilation mechanisms, downdraft motors, exhaust ductwork connections, and control systems coordinating cooktop and ventilation. Common issues include ventilation not rising, weak airflow, and motor failures. Our technicians service both the cooking surface and integrated ventilation system for complete downdraft cooktop functionality.</p>

                                <h4 style="color: var(--blue); margin: 15px 0 10px;">Modular Cooktop Repair</h4>
                                <p style="margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Electrolux modular cooktop repair</strong> services customizable cooking systems with interchangeable cooking modules. These configurations allow combining gas, electric, induction, and specialty modules. We repair individual module components, shared control systems, and the connections between modules. Common issues include individual modules failing while others work, control synchronization problems, and power distribution failures. Our technicians understand modular system integration for comprehensive repair.</p>

                                <h4 style="color: var(--blue); margin: 15px 0 10px;">FlexInduction Cooktop Repair</h4>
                                <p style="margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Electrolux FlexInduction cooktop repair</strong> addresses the advanced flexible cooking zones that combine multiple induction areas into larger surfaces. FlexInduction allows using large cookware across combined zones. We repair zone linking controls, multiple induction coils, and the electronics enabling flexible zone configuration. Common issues include zones not combining properly, power distribution errors, and cookware detection failures across linked zones. Our technicians restore full FlexInduction flexibility.</p>

                                <h4 style="color: var(--blue); margin: 15px 0 10px;">Smart Cooktop Repair</h4>
                                <p style="margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Electrolux smart cooktop repair</strong> includes Home Connect WiFi features for remote monitoring and integration with Electrolux hoods for automatic ventilation activation. Smart cooktops communicate with connected hoods to adjust fan speed based on cooking intensity. We repair control boards enabling connectivity, diagnose pairing problems, and service all heating components. Our technicians address both smart features and traditional cooktop repairs for comprehensive service.</p>

                            </div>
